CRITICAL FIX: Media nodes now clickable (3rd level content)

ROOT CAUSE:
Defensive guard was blocking all media clicks due to check order.
Media nodes have 'mediaId' field, not 'id' field.
Guard checked for 'id' existence BEFORE checking 'isMedia' flag.
Result: All media node clicks rejected with "Node missing ID" warning.

THE BUG:
```javascript
// BEFORE (BROKEN):
const nodeData = node.userData;
if (!nodeData.id) {           // ← Media nodes don't have 'id'!
  console.warn('Missing ID');
  return;                     // ← Exits before checking isMedia
}
if (nodeData.isMedia) {       // ← Never reached for media nodes
  setSelectedMedia(nodeData);
}
```

THE FIX:
```javascript
// AFTER (FIXED):
const nodeData = node.userData;
if (nodeData.isMedia) {       // ← Check media FIRST
  setSelectedMedia(nodeData);
  return;
}
if (!nodeData.id) {           // ← Then check ID for regular nodes
  console.warn('Missing ID');
  return;
}
```

IMPACT:
- Media orbs (3rd level) now open viewer modal when clicked
- All 100+ media items now accessible
- Videos, images, documents, articles all viewable
- Full content finally reachable

TEST:
1. Expand any methodology (e.g., Scenarios)
2. Click any colored media orb
3. Modal should open with media details
4. Click background or X to close

This was the "nodes not popping open" issue - defensive code
was too defensive and blocked legitimate media clicks.

